onnect version is changing  or when the connect api version is  changing so that's that's really the  time to be careful and to pay attention  but generally speaking  it should work  most of the time um  and by most of the time i mean like  there are edge cases right and those are  not super likely but  again we try to note them here if and  when they do appear  but um but yeah this is also one of the  pressures that has been keeping us off  of crayon a little bit is trying to  trying to get things as stable as  possible until before we put things um  out there on crayon forever  thanks cole  thank you so much for your presentation  too and sharing this with us i am i  don't see other questions but i want to  make sure that i haven't missed anything  across  linkedin twitter or youtube  i think we're all set on slido  let me double check the chat  and as i mentioned we're happy to use  this time to answer other questions  about connect2 while we're here  but cool i think it would be helpful to  if we could go back to the slide where  you kind of talked about next steps and  where people can go to  continue the conversation too  yes  yes so um so yeah so this link here is  uh just  the community uh thread that rachel  started um so again this is  maybe a harder url to remember  but inside of community if you're inside  of community an easy way to find um the  place where a lot of connect questions  are asked if you're curious you want to  see what other people are talking about  is if you go to our admins  so  perhaps a uh not as great named  name for a category now that we have  python admins right  um but if you go to r admins and then  our studio connect  this section is uh where a lot of these  types of questions are most welcome  you'll see my face a lot uh  unfortunately but this thread that  rachel started is right here  and so there's uh community.org.com and  then the links are in the discussion  thread here  but that um  that's a really good place to kind o